-- The shape of the `ssr` lowering's output (backend.md §15.1, §15.2,
-- §15.6). Each root's static text is its kind, hoisted after the imports
-- and named by its site, `<Module>$k<instruction>`: a root with no dynamic
-- part is its whole block, `{ t: … }`, built once; any other root is an
-- array of static strings its block concatenates with its values. Each
-- value is bound to a `const` where the root is evaluated, in source order,
-- unless it is already a name. A `For` row compiled in place is a function
-- the runtime's `list` calls per item, and its body is a root of its own.
-- The runtime's exports are imported once each, beside `html`'s primitive.
import Html exposing (Html)


pub static : Html msg
static = <p class="lead">Hello &amp; welcome</p>


pub greet : { name : String, count : Int } -> Html msg
greet user = <p title={user.name}>Hi {user.name}, {user.count} new<br />{Html.text "!"}</p>


pub list : List String -> Html msg
list items = <ul><For each={items}>{\item -> <li>{item}</li>}</For></ul>
